# QC workflow rules

- Work only on this synthetic portfolio. Never use third-party customer systems, secrets, production URLs or real PII.
- Before writing code or tests, map requirement `BR-XX`, risk, happy path, negative path, boundary values and state transition.
- Use `TC-<MODULE>-<NNN>` IDs and document preconditions, data, steps and measurable expected results.
- Separate test levels: pure domain, HTTP API, Playwright UI and manual/exploratory charters.
- Treat money and webhook integrity as high risk: validate signature, amount, event IDs, state, replay behavior and inventory.
- Use isolated servers and fake data; never run destructive live actions.
- If an assertion fails, document expected vs actual and evidence. Never edit the expected outcome solely to turn a failure green.
- Every run summary includes executed tests, pass/fail/blocked/not-run, environment, evidence and residual risk.
- Prefer deterministic automated smoke/regression via npm scripts; MCP is optional for local exploration, not a replacement for saved test evidence.
- AI/agent output is a draft requiring human QA review and can never claim unexecuted tests passed.
